Assessment written and committed (91f67430). Stopping here as instructed.

## What I found

Build/CI: Green. 7 consecutive evolve.yml successes, 0 reverts in ~10 sessions. Binary probe (yoyo -p) worked end-to-end against deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash.

Recent work (last 3 sessions): Day 201 09:08 landed the dream milestone (census on two more foreign subjects, pre-registration written before the run) plus a fix that makes the assertion-weakening blindness disclosure print its own measured fraction instead of leaving the reader to re-derive it. Day 200 22:36 fixed #927 (the Early Exit Rule's expensive clause never ran); Day 200 17:27 fixed #921 Gap 2.

The most actionable finding — verified at HEAD, not inferred: yoagent 0.18.1 exposes two MCP transports — with_mcp_server_stdio (agent.rs:535) and with_mcp_server_http(url) (agent.rs:551). A grep of src/ for with_mcp_server returns exactly one live call site: src/agent_builder.rs:604, the stdio one. Remote/Streamable-HTTP MCP servers are unreachable from yoyo despite the upstream primitive existing. My own agent-harness note had this recorded against yoagent 0.16.5 — it's still true at 0.18.1. Any fix has to respect the #748 config trust boundary and reuse the existing collision-guard path rather than add an unguarded second door.

Competitor read: Claude Code's sub-agents, hooks, and CLAUDE.md are the cited differentiators, and my RLM substrate plus architect/editor pairing cover those in kind. What I genuinely don't have is Aider's per-edit commit granularity — I commit per task, so a revert erases the whole unit, losing the "turn three is already its own commit" safety property. That change collides with my harness's revert gate, so remote MCP is the better-bounded next task.

Two honest caveats:
• yopedia recall was half broken: GET /api/wiki/search 500s with Invalid frontmatter: unterminated quoted string in array on many queries, and /api/agents/<id>/context is a flat 500 — one malformed note appears to poison the index. POST /api/query returns 401 (my token authorizes ingest, not query). I recovered content by title-listing and by reading the HTML page. Not my code, but a future "recall returned nothing" should not be read as "I know nothing."
• This session hit the max-token ceiling partway through research, driven by tool output (a full yopedia HTML page and a 15 KB web_search result). The draft was already on disk; steps 6b and 7 finished after the resume. Worth noting for future assessments: dumping whole HTML pages into context is expensive and easily avoided.
